1. a plain client
  login: USER refused: 530 Login only after AUTH TLS., control encrypted: 0, data encrypted: 0
2. explicit FTPS (AUTH TLS, then PBSZ 0 and PROT P)
  login: ok, control encrypted: 1, data encrypted: 1
  stored and fetched back: for your eyes only
    C: AUTH TLS
    C: PBSZ 0
    C: PROT P
    C: PASS ****
3. implicit FTPS on the second port
  login: ok, control encrypted: 1, data encrypted: 1
  stored and fetched back: for your eyes only
    C: PBSZ 0
    C: PROT P
    C: PASS ****
4. the client skips PROT P, the server insists on it
  login: ok, control encrypted: 1, data encrypted: 0
  store failed: PASV failed: 522 Data connections must be encrypted (PROT P).
    C: AUTH TLS
    C: PASS ****
